The experimental procedure began with a 20-minute initial polarization period under the 10 V DC supply, from which the collected data were used to generate the electrical resistivity curves and identify the percolation threshold of the composites using the Percolation Theory Power Law presented in Eq.  4  [ 36 ]. In this equation, σ is the electrical conductivity of the composite, σ 0  is a scaling factor related to the intrinsic conductivity of the filler,  φ  is the percentage of CNT content,  φ crit  is the percolation threshold content, and t is the critical exponent. 4 \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
